    "conclusion": "Giving the blanket to Rowan (Action A) is uniquely defensible because the strongest reasonable rejection falls on the alternative principle that would give the blanket to Sasha.",
    "strongest_objection": "Sasha reasonably objects that she faces certain death under Action A while she would have a 60 % survival chance under Action B.",
    "answer_to_objection": "Rowan’s symmetrical objection under Action B is even stronger, since he would lose an 80 % survival chance, making Sasha’s objection insufficient to overturn the comparison.",
    "reversal_condition": "If the survival probabilities were equal, or Sasha’s survival advantage exceeded Rowan’s lost chance (e.g., 90 % vs 50 %), Sasha’s complaint could become strongest, reversing the recommendation.",
    "residual_disagreement": [
      "Whether a 20 % difference in lost survival chance is enough to make one complaint decisively stronger remains open to reasonable dispute."
    ]
